  "worked_solution": "Notice that the given approximation can be written using exponents as:\n\n$$\n{e}^{1/3}≈1.396\n$$\n\nThe natural logarithm of $a$ is defined as follows:\n\n$a={e}^{x}$ is equivalent to $\\operatorname{ln}⁡a=x$ \n\nIf we compare ${e}^{1/3}≈1.396$ with $a={e}^{x},$ we get $a=1.396$ and $x=\\frac{1}{3}.$ \n\nTherefore, the approximation $\\sqrt[3]{e}≈1.396$ can be expressed as $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.396)≈\\frac{1}{3}.$",
